---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import features from "../data/features.json";
---
<SiteLayout title="Retail POS Mobile — A clearer way to run the counter" description="An independent Android-first retail POS in development, shaped around everyday shop workflows, traceable stock, and an honest offline-first design." path="/">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <span class="hero-kicker"><span class="status-dot"></span> ANDROID POS · IN DEVELOPMENT</span>
        <h1>Less friction at the counter.<br /><span>More clarity behind it.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">We’re building an Android-first POS around the real rhythm of small retail: a focused checkout, traceable stock, and a thoughtful plan for unreliable connectivity.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/product/">Explore the product <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/features/">See what’s planned <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-proof-row">
          <span>Built for small-shop workflows</span>
          <span>PKR context · Pakistan</span>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">Pre-launch project. No public APK is available yet.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-visual" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative product map, not a screenshot of a released app. It shows four planned capability areas: checkout, stock history, till control, and offline sync.">
        <div class="visual-backdrop" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="visual-frame">
          <div class="visual-frame-top">
            <div>
              <span class="visual-overline">The product, at a glance</span>
              <h2 class="visual-heading">Everyday retail.<br />In clearer focus.</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="visual-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          </div>
          <div class="visual-map" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="visual-core">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect x="5" y="4" width="22" height="24" rx="6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/>
                <path d="M10 11h12M10 16h8M10 21h5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                <circle cx="23" cy="22" r="2" fill="#5eead4"/>
              </svg>
              <strong>Retail POS</strong>
              <small>Mobile</small>
            </div>
            <div class="visual-node visual-node-checkout">
              <span class="visual-node-mark">01</span>
              <span><strong>Checkout</strong><small>Planned workflow</small></span>
            </div>
            <div class="visual-node visual-node-stock">
              <span class="visual-node-mark">02</span>
              <span><strong>Stock history</strong><small>Planned workflow</small></span>
            </div>
            <div class="visual-node visual-node-till">
              <span class="visual-node-mark">03</span>
              <span><strong>Till control</strong><small>Planned workflow</small></span>
            </div>
            <div class="visual-node visual-node-sync">
              <span class="visual-node-mark">04</span>
              <span><strong>Offline & sync</strong><small>Design goal</small></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="visual-frame-bottom">
            <span>Independent Android-first product</span>
            <span class="visual-status">FOUNDATION STAGE</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="visual-caption">Illustrative product map — not a screenshot of a released app.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="trust-strip">
    <div class="container trust-strip-inner">
      <p><strong>Thoughtful by design.</strong> Built around everyday work, with honest status at every stage.</p>
      <div class="trust-items">
        <span>Clear counter flows</span>
        <span>Traceable operations</span>
        <span>Safer sync by design</span>
        <span>No inflated claims</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">01 / Product direction</span>
          <h2>The everyday work, thought through.</h2>
          <p>These are the capability areas the product is being built toward. Each remains planned until implementation and release checks provide real evidence.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/">Explore all planned features <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid">
        {features.map((feature,index)=><article class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{String(index+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span>
          <span class="status-pill status-planned"><span class="status-dot"></span> Planned</span>
          <h3>{feature.title}</h3>
          <p>{feature.outcome}</p>
          <a class="text-link" href={feature.id==="offline"?"/offline-first/":"/features/"}>Explore scope <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="container split-panel">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">02 / Offline, without pretending</span>
        <h2>Disconnected devices can’t know what each other just sold.</h2>
        <p>The plan is to queue local work safely, retry without duplicating transactions, and make conflicts visible for review instead of silently rewriting sales history.</p>
        <p>This is an architecture goal, not a released capability. It must be implemented and tested before we describe it as available.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/offline-first/">Read the offline approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="architecture-card">
        <span class="status-pill status-planned"><span class="status-dot"></span> Planned architecture</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top:18px">A clear path from local work to sync.</h3>
        <p>Three boundaries make the intended approach easier to understand.</p>
        <div class="flow-stack">
          <div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">01</span><div><strong>On-device data</strong><small>Fast local access for supported workflows</small></div></div>
          <div class="flow-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">02</span><div><strong>Durable outbox</strong><small>Queue operations for safe retry and reconciliation</small></div></div>
          <div class="flow-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-number">03</span><div><strong>Independent cloud backend</strong><small>Validate and reconcile when connectivity returns</small></div></div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:18px;font-size:.8rem">Conceptual architecture only; not a claim that these workflows are released.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-band">
        <div>
          <span class="visual-overline">03 / Release status</span>
          <h2>A real build deserves real release notes.</h2>
          <p>When an approved signed APK exists, the download page will show its exact version, build, Android requirements, checksum, and known limitations. Until then, we’ll keep the status clear.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button" href="/download/">View release status <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
